       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults under supervision, and four times the OTC limit of 1,200 mg/day. It would put the patient at serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **1600 mg/day total**, divided, for example 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily\n\nIf 1600 mg four times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
